# Claude Code / second-shift local session telemetry — per-run audit hook logs.
# Never version-controlled: machine-local, regenerated each run, pure noise in diffs.
.claude/audit/

# dev-pipeline run state — machine-local per-ticket state files (incl. this repo's
# own canary/dogfooding runs). Transient; the default paths.pipelineStateDir.
.claude/pipeline-state/

# dev-pipeline linked worktrees — the pipeline creates its own git worktrees here
# (work branches, intake-pin) when this is a locally-configured worktreesDir location.
# The shipped default worktreesDir is ../<repo>-worktrees (outside the tree).
# Machine-local and registered as git worktrees, but an untracked entry here still makes
# `git status --porcelain` non-empty, which mis-records the pre-flight attestation
# (workingTreeClean) on this repo's own dogfooding runs. Ignore it so the pipeline's own
# artifacts never read as a dirty tree. (Surfaced by the #1 dogfooding retro.)
.claude/worktrees/

# Lean-lane design render output — the screenshots `lean-gate.sh` milestone 3 captures for a
# design-armed ticket. The bytes never enter history; the committed evidence is the hash
# manifest at <plansDir>/<key>-lean-renders.md. The gate asserts this path is ignored BEFORE it
# renders and prints this exact line when it is not, so the rule is part of the contract rather
# than a courtesy. Present here even though this repo declares no design.provider — the
# assertion is on the output path, not on what happens to be in the tree.
.claude/lean-renders/

# The operator's machine-local Claude allowlist. Ignored here rather than only in a personal
# global ignore file, because `lean-gate.sh entry` COPIES it into each lane worktree (#647) and
# refuses to when the destination path is not ignored — an untracked file there would make
# `git status --porcelain` non-empty, and that is the predicate the entry sweep and the
# scheduler's in-flight boundary both read to decide whether a lane worktree still holds work.
# A worktree the gate itself dirtied is one the reaper never removes again. `.claude/settings.json`
# is deliberately NOT here: it is tracked, so a worktree already carries it.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-machine direnv env (OTel telemetry export for cost tracking) — local-only,
# opt-in per engineer; see the dev-pipeline plugin's cost-tracking-setup.md.
.envrc

# This repo's own dogfooding config — carries real, machine-local bot/app identifiers
# (GitHub App clientId/appName/installationId + private-key path). Same per-machine class
# as the ignored paths above; must never ship in the public marketplace (trace gate denylists
# these tokens). Keep it on disk locally for self-consumption runs; do not version it.
.claude/second-shift.config.json
